    <h2>Watermark Guard — Full Guide</h2>
    <p>AI platforms may embed two kinds of provenance marks. This panel attacks both — with honest limits.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><td>1 · Metadata tags</td><td>Strings in the file container: ID3 "generated by Suno", C2PA/Content Credentials, iXML, bext. <b>Removed automatically</b> — every export is a fresh encode with your © / ISRC instead.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2 · Signal watermarks</td><td>Inaudible patterns woven into the audio: spread-spectrum noise (often near Nyquist), echo hiding (micro-delays), phase coding. The tools below attack these.</td></tr>
    </table>
    <table>
      <tr><td>WM LPF</td><td><b>What:</b> low-pass 15–19.8 kHz, cutting ultrasonic spread-spectrum energy. <b>Use:</b> ~17–18k for AI sources. <b>Cost:</b> slightly duller extreme top.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ULTRA LPF</td><td>Enables/disables that filter. Leave ON for AI tracks.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>RESAMP RT</td><td><b>What:</b> resamples 44.1↔48 kHz at export — interpolation breaks phase/echo codes that depend on exact sample timing. <b>Cost:</b> negligible, quality-transparent.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LOSSY RT</td><td><b>What:</b> MP3 320 encode/decode at export — discards low-level detail where fragile marks hide. <b>Use:</b> strongest scrub for known-watermarked sources. <b>Cost:</b> a hair of sheen; audition first.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>🎧 AUDITION MP3</td><td>Plays the master through a real MP3 320 round-trip on B. Always audition before export.</td></tr>
    </table>
    <p><b>Workflow:</b> ① check metadata chip → ② WM LPF 17.5k → ③ master → ④ RESAMP RT on, LOSSY RT if needed → ⑤ 🎧 audition → ⚡ → ⬇.</p>
    <div class="warnbx"><b>Honest limits:</b> robust watermarks are engineered to survive this — the panel degrades them, it cannot guarantee removal. Removing provenance marks to misrepresent AI music as human-made may violate platform ToS or disclosure law.</div>

